-- DIMENSION 1: ADAPTABILITY & LEARNING AGILITY
(1,'adaptability_learning','Change Embrace','Your team switches to a new project management platform with two weeks notice. In the first week, what would most accurately describe your experience?','situational','likert_5','rating_scale','I spend time exploring it on my own and pick it up quickly','I follow the training provided and get up to speed within the deadline','I feel frustrated but push through and learn what I need','I rely on a colleague to help me with the parts I find difficult','I master the basics but need more time for advanced features',false,false,'{"1":5,"2":4,"3":3,"4":2,"5":3}',0.25),

(2,'adaptability_learning','Learning Speed','Think about the last time you had to learn something new at work without formal training. Which best describes what happened?','behavioral_frequency','likert_5','rating_scale','I waited until someone could walk me through it','I found relevant documentation and worked through it methodically','I experimented, made mistakes, and figured it out through trial and error','I asked a colleague to show me, then practiced independently','I watched a tutorial once and felt confident immediately',false,false,'{"1":1,"2":4,"3":5,"4":4,"5":2}',0.25),

(3,'adaptability_learning','Ambiguity Tolerance','Which of these two statements is MORE like how you typically work?','attitudinal','choice_best_worst','forced_choice','I do my best thinking when I have enough structure to work within','I do my best thinking when I have the freedom to define my own approach',NULL,NULL,NULL,false,false,'{"1":3,"2":5}',0.25),

(4,'adaptability_learning','Problem Solving','A process critical to your work breaks down on a Friday afternoon. IT support is unavailable until Monday. What do you do?','situational','likert_5','rating_scale','Document what happened, create a temporary workaround, and flag it for Monday','Reach out to IT or a colleague who might know the system, even outside hours','Pause the work affected and pick it up when the issue is resolved Monday','Search online resources and try to resolve it myself before giving up','Escalate to my manager and ask them to find a solution',false,false,'{"1":5,"2":4,"3":2,"4":4,"5":2}',0.25),

(5,'adaptability_learning','Change Embrace','When a well-established process you rely on is replaced by a new one, which most accurately reflects your typical pattern over the following month?','behavioral_frequency','likert_5','rating_scale','I take longer than my peers to reach the same comfort level','I reach competence at roughly the same pace as my colleagues','I get to grips with it faster than most, though I still have questions','I find the transition straightforward and help others who are struggling','I invest extra time upfront so I can become a resource for the team',false,false,'{"1":1,"2":3,"3":4,"4":5,"5":5}',0.25),

(6,'adaptability_learning','Learning Speed','You are given an important project that requires a skill you have not used before. Your deadline is in three weeks. Which response most closely matches yours?','situational','likert_5','rating_scale','I immediately identify what I need to learn and build a rapid development plan','I assess the gap, source learning materials, and practice while delivering','I request extra time and ask for someone to mentor me through it','I complete what I can and flag the skill gap to my manager early','I feel uncertain but commit to figuring it out as I go',false,false,'{"1":5,"2":5,"3":3,"4":3,"5":2}',0.25),

(7,'adaptability_learning','Ambiguity Tolerance','Which of these two statements is MORE like how you feel when starting a new project?','attitudinal','choice_best_worst','forced_choice','I feel most effective when I know exactly what success looks like from the start','I feel most effective when I can shape what success looks like as I learn more',NULL,NULL,NULL,false,false,'{"1":2,"2":5}',0.25),

(8,'adaptability_learning','Problem Solving','Looking back at the last six months of your work, how would you characterise your approach to the tasks you completed?','behavioral_frequency','likert_5','rating_scale','I primarily followed established procedures and escalated exceptions','I mostly followed procedures but occasionally suggested improvements','I followed procedures where they worked well and created alternatives where they did not','I regularly evaluated existing procedures and introduced better ways when I found them','I treated most procedures as starting points and routinely built on or replaced them',false,false,NULL,0.25),

(9,'adaptability_learning','Change Embrace','A significant shift in your industry requires you to develop expertise in an area outside your current skill set. Which response best matches your typical approach?','situational','likert_5','rating_scale','I sign up for a formal course and work through it systematically','I read broadly across multiple sources and form my own synthesis','I find someone already working in this area and learn through conversation','I wait until my employer provides specific guidance or training','I start applying the new concepts to current work immediately to learn by doing',false,false,'{"1":4,"2":4,"3":4,"4":1,"5":5}',0.25),

(10,'adaptability_learning','Change Embrace','Thinking honestly about your career so far, which statement is most accurate?','attitudinal','likert_5','rating_scale','There have been several changes at work that I struggled to adapt to initially','There have been one or two significant changes that took me longer than expected to adjust to','I generally adapt without much difficulty, though some situations challenge me','I adapt quickly in most situations and rarely find change difficult','I have never had a meaningful difficulty adapting to any change at work',false,true,'{"1":5,"2":5,"3":4,"4":3,"5":1}',0.25),

-- DIMENSION 2: INITIATIVE & OWNERSHIP
(11,'initiative_ownership','Self-Direction','When working on a multi-week project, how do you typically manage your relationship with your manager?','behavioral_frequency','likert_5','rating_scale','I provide regular updates without waiting to be asked and flag issues early','I send updates at key milestones and check in when I hit a blocker','I update my manager when I have something worth reporting','I wait for my manager to check in, then provide a status','I prefer to work independently and present a completed result',false,false,'{"1":5,"2":5,"3":3,"4":2,"5":3}',0.30),

(12,'initiative_ownership','Proactive Behavior','You notice a recurring inefficiency that frustrates the whole team but does not fall within anyone''s defined responsibilities. Which response is most like yours?','situational','likert_5','rating_scale','I raise it in the next team meeting as something worth addressing','I speak to my manager privately and suggest we look into it','I investigate the root cause on my own and bring a proposed fix','I mention it informally to a colleague but wait to see if leadership addresses it','I resolve what I can within my own scope and document what requires broader action',false,false,'{"1":3,"2":3,"3":5,"4":1,"5":4}',0.25),

(13,'initiative_ownership','Accountability','A project you led misses a key deliverable due to a combination of your decisions and team execution issues. How do you respond to leadership?','situational','likert_5','rating_scale','I present a clear account of what happened, own my decisions, and outline the recovery plan','I explain the contributing factors honestly, including my own role, and ask for guidance','I present the facts objectively without emphasising individual contributions','I describe the team challenges while acknowledging my own decisions played a part','I outline what the team could have done differently and what I will change next time',false,false,'{"1":5,"2":4,"3":2,"4":3,"5":3}',0.25),

(14,'initiative_ownership','Resource Optimization','Your project budget is cut by 30% one month before launch. What is your typical first response?','situational','likert_5','rating_scale','Immediately identify what can be cut without affecting core outcomes','Negotiate with stakeholders to clarify which outcomes are non-negotiable','Request additional budget justification and escalate to leadership','Re-sequence deliverables so critical items are protected within the new budget','Consult the team on where savings can be found before making any decisions',false,false,'{"1":5,"2":4,"3":2,"4":5,"5":4}',0.20),

(15,'initiative_ownership','Self-Direction','Which of these two statements is MORE like how you prefer to work?','attitudinal','choice_best_worst','forced_choice','I prefer to agree on a clear goal upfront and then determine my own path to it','I prefer to agree on a clear goal upfront and then follow an established process to reach it',NULL,NULL,NULL,false,false,'{"1":5,"2":2}',0.30),

(16,'initiative_ownership','Proactive Behavior','In the past year, how many times have you initiated a process improvement or new initiative at work without being asked?','behavioral_frequency','likert_5','rating_scale','Not that I can recall','Once or twice — small suggestions that were adopted','Two or three times — some led to meaningful changes','Several times — I regularly look for things to improve','Frequently — improving processes is a natural part of how I work',false,false,NULL,0.25),

(17,'initiative_ownership','Accountability','When something goes wrong on a project, which of these is more like your instinctive first response?','attitudinal','choice_best_worst','forced_choice','Understanding what I could have done differently, even before knowing all the facts','Understanding all the contributing factors before drawing any conclusions about my role',NULL,NULL,NULL,false,false,'{"1":5,"2":3}',0.25),

(18,'initiative_ownership','Resource Optimization','When you have had to deliver a project with fewer resources than you felt were needed, what outcome did you most commonly achieve?','behavioral_frequency','likert_5','rating_scale','Delivered a reduced scope with the available resources','Delivered the full scope but with lower quality than planned','Delivered the full scope on time by finding creative alternatives','Delivered the full scope and identified savings that carried forward','Requested additional resources before committing to the original scope',false,false,'{"1":2,"2":2,"3":4,"4":5,"5":1}',0.20),

(19,'initiative_ownership','Self-Direction','Your manager announces an unexpected two-week absence. No interim cover is assigned. How would your work output most likely be affected?','situational','likert_5','rating_scale','No meaningful impact — I operate with the same independence as normal','Slight disruption on decisions that typically need approval, otherwise fine','I can handle day-to-day work but would pause anything requiring significant judgment','I would reach out to other senior colleagues for guidance on most decisions','I would document all pending decisions and wait for my manager to return for direction',false,false,'{"1":5,"2":4,"3":3,"4":2,"5":1}',0.30),

(20,'initiative_ownership','Proactive Behavior','Thinking honestly about your work habits, which statement is most accurate?','attitudinal','likert_5','rating_scale','I sometimes put off tasks that are complex or outside my comfort zone','I occasionally delay starting things I find difficult until I feel more ready','I generally start tasks promptly but sometimes procrastinate on the harder ones','I rarely procrastinate and usually start tasks as soon as I can','I have never procrastinated on an important work task',false,true,'{"1":5,"2":5,"3":4,"4":3,"5":1}',0.25),

-- DIMENSION 3: COLLABORATION & TEAM DYNAMICS
(21,'collaboration_team','Communication','In a team meeting where multiple people have conflicting views, which role do you most naturally take?','situational','likert_5','rating_scale','I listen carefully and ask questions to understand all perspectives before contributing','I share my view clearly and directly, then actively invite others to challenge it','I look for the threads of agreement and help synthesise a shared position','I contribute when I have something specific to add, otherwise I let others lead','I often end up summarising the discussion and helping the group reach a decision',false,false,'{"1":4,"2":4,"3":5,"4":2,"5":5}',0.30),

(22,'collaboration_team','Team Support','A colleague is significantly behind on a deliverable that will affect the team. You are also stretched. What do you do?','situational','likert_5','rating_scale','I talk to them to understand what is causing the delay and offer to help with specific parts','I let my manager know about the risk and suggest a plan to redistribute work','I focus on my own deliverables but keep an eye on whether the team will be impacted','I offer general support but wait to see how bad it gets before taking action','I adjust my own schedule to take on some of their work without being asked',false,false,'{"1":5,"2":4,"3":2,"4":1,"5":4}',0.25),

(23,'collaboration_team','Conflict Resolution','A colleague implements a solution that you are confident will create problems downstream. How do you handle it?','situational','likert_5','rating_scale','I raise my concern directly with them, explain my reasoning, and listen to their response','I document my concern in writing and share it with the relevant people','I ask them to walk me through their thinking to see if I am missing something','I mention it to my manager and let them decide whether to intervene','I voice my disagreement clearly in the next team meeting so it is on record',false,false,'{"1":5,"2":3,"3":5,"4":2,"5":3}',0.20),

(24,'collaboration_team','Cross-Functional Work','Reflecting on your experience working with teams from other departments, which best describes your typical experience?','behavioral_frequency','likert_5','rating_scale','I find it takes meaningful effort to navigate the different priorities and communication styles','I can work across teams but find it slower and less efficient than working within my own team','I am equally comfortable working cross-functionally as within my own team','I find cross-functional work stimulating and often produce better outcomes with diverse teams','I actively seek out cross-functional collaborations because of the different perspectives they bring',false,false,NULL,0.25),

(25,'collaboration_team','Communication','Which of these two statements is MORE true of how you work at your best?','attitudinal','choice_best_worst','forced_choice','I produce my strongest work through regular collaboration and dialogue with colleagues','I produce my strongest work through focused, uninterrupted independent effort',NULL,NULL,NULL,false,false,'{"1":5,"2":2}',0.30),

(26,'collaboration_team','Team Support','When you develop a useful technique, process, or piece of knowledge at work, what do you typically do with it?','behavioral_frequency','likert_5','rating_scale','I document it and proactively share it with anyone who might benefit','I share it when someone asks or when a relevant situation comes up','I use it myself and mention it informally if it seems relevant to someone nearby','I keep it in my personal notes and apply it to my own work','I rarely formalise what I learn in a way that I could share',false,false,'{"1":5,"2":4,"3":3,"4":2,"5":1}',0.25),

(27,'collaboration_team','Conflict Resolution','When faced with tension between two colleagues, which of these is more like your natural response?','attitudinal','choice_best_worst','forced_choice','I tend to engage directly to help resolve the issue, even if it is uncomfortable','I tend to give them space and let them work it out unless asked to get involved',NULL,NULL,NULL,false,false,'{"1":5,"2":2}',0.20),

(28,'collaboration_team','Cross-Functional Work','You are asked to lead a project involving four departments, each with competing priorities. What is your typical first step?','situational','likert_5','rating_scale','Map each department''s priorities and find areas of genuine alignment before any kickoff','Set up a shared kickoff meeting, align on a common goal, and agree on decision-making rules','Identify the senior stakeholder in each department and get their buy-in individually','Start with the most critical workstream and manage cross-functional dependencies as they arise','Delegate a coordination role to someone in each department to manage their team''s involvement',false,false,'{"1":4,"2":5,"3":3,"4":3,"5":2}',0.25),

(29,'collaboration_team','Communication','After an important team meeting, how do you typically ensure alignment on next steps?','behavioral_frequency','likert_5','rating_scale','I send a written summary of decisions and action items to all attendees','I verbally confirm the key decisions before the meeting ends','I follow up with the people whose actions depend on mine','I trust that people noted what they need to do','I check in a day or two later if I notice things are not moving',false,false,'{"1":5,"2":4,"3":3,"4":1,"5":2}',0.30),

(30,'collaboration_team','Team Support','Thinking honestly about your working relationships, which statement is most accurate?','attitudinal','likert_5','rating_scale','There have been colleagues I have found genuinely difficult to work with over a sustained period','I have had one or two working relationships that required significant effort to manage','Most of my working relationships are positive, though some take more energy than others','I generally get along well with colleagues and rarely find relationships challenging','I have never had a meaningful difficulty working with any colleague',false,true,'{"1":5,"2":5,"3":4,"4":3,"5":1}',0.25),

-- DIMENSION 4: RESILIENCE & STRESS MANAGEMENT
(31,'resilience_stress','Stress Tolerance','You are managing three projects simultaneously when a fourth urgent one is added. Which best describes how this typically affects your output?','situational','likert_5','rating_scale','I reprioritise clearly, communicate trade-offs to stakeholders, and maintain quality across all','I handle the load but one project typically receives less attention than the others','I work longer hours to absorb the extra demand and maintain all commitments','Quality dips on at least one project but I meet deadlines','I push back on the fourth project until capacity frees up',false,false,'{"1":5,"2":3,"3":4,"4":2,"5":3}',0.30),

(32,'resilience_stress','Emotional Stability','Think about the last significant setback you experienced at work. How long did it affect your attitude and energy?','behavioral_frequency','likert_5','rating_scale','It affected me for several weeks and I found it hard to refocus','It weighed on me for about a week before I could move on fully','It bothered me for a couple of days, then I refocused','I processed it quickly — within a day I was back to my normal pace','It barely affected me — I treated it as information and moved on immediately',false,false,NULL,0.25),

(33,'resilience_stress','Recovery Speed','After receiving critical or negative feedback on something you worked hard on, which best describes your usual pattern?','behavioral_frequency','likert_5','rating_scale','I feel defensive initially but work through it over several days','I feel disappointed but actively seek to understand and apply the feedback','I process it quickly and identify two or three concrete changes I can make','I feel motivated by the gap it reveals and start improving immediately','I rarely have a strong emotional reaction — I treat it as useful data',false,false,'{"1":2,"2":3,"3":4,"4":5,"5":4}',0.20),

(34,'resilience_stress','Optimism','Your organisation announces it is facing its toughest year commercially. Your team is under pressure. What best describes your outlook and behaviour over the following month?','situational','likert_5','rating_scale','I acknowledge the difficulty, focus on what I can control, and maintain my output','I feel anxious about job security but manage to keep working effectively','I find it motivating — this is when people show what they are made of','I am cautious and wait to see how things develop before changing how I work','I am concerned but try not to let it affect my team''s morale',false,false,'{"1":5,"2":2,"3":5,"4":2,"5":4}',0.25),

(35,'resilience_stress','Stress Tolerance','Which of these two statements is MORE like how you experience high-pressure periods at work?','attitudinal','choice_best_worst','forced_choice','Pressure tends to sharpen my focus and I often do my best work under tight deadlines','Pressure is a normal part of work and I manage it by staying disciplined about priorities',NULL,NULL,NULL,false,false,'{"1":5,"2":4}',0.30),

(36,'resilience_stress','Emotional Stability','How would your closest colleague most accurately describe your demeanour across a typical month that includes both good weeks and difficult weeks?','behavioral_frequency','likert_5','rating_scale','Noticeably different — they would observe real highs and lows','Slightly variable — my mood is readable but I manage it','Generally consistent — they see some variation but I do not bring stress to the team','Very consistent — people rarely know if I am having a difficult week','Remarkably steady — colleagues sometimes ask how I stay so even',false,false,NULL,0.25),

(37,'resilience_stress','Recovery Speed','Which of these two statements is MORE like how you relate to past mistakes?','attitudinal','choice_best_worst','forced_choice','I analyse what went wrong, extract the lesson, and then move on relatively quickly','I reflect on what went wrong carefully and make sure I fully understand it before moving on',NULL,NULL,NULL,false,false,'{"1":5,"2":4}',0.20),

(38,'resilience_stress','Optimism','When you encounter a significant obstacle on a project, what is your most common initial response?','behavioral_frequency','likert_5','rating_scale','I feel frustrated but take time to think through solutions','I assess the obstacle quickly and start generating options','I immediately involve others to bring more perspectives to the problem','I communicate the obstacle upward and look for a decision on how to proceed','I look for what I can continue working on while the obstacle is being addressed',false,false,'{"1":3,"2":5,"3":4,"4":2,"5":4}',0.25),

(39,'resilience_stress','Stress Tolerance','Your team loses two members unexpectedly, temporarily doubling your workload. Over the following month, which outcome is most realistic for you?','situational','likert_5','rating_scale','I manage it — I work harder, reprioritise ruthlessly, and deliver what matters most','I absorb most of the extra load but quality suffers in some areas','I maintain my quality but need to extend some deadlines','I flag the capacity issue early, agree on a reduced scope, and deliver that well','I struggle significantly and need management intervention to manage expectations',false,false,'{"1":5,"2":3,"3":3,"4":5,"5":1}',0.30),

(40,'resilience_stress','Emotional Stability','Thinking honestly about how you handle stress, which statement is most accurate?','attitudinal','likert_5','rating_scale','There are certain types of work pressure that reliably affect my mood or performance','I have specific triggers that I am aware of and actively manage','I manage stress well overall, though some situations are genuinely hard','I rarely feel meaningfully stressed by work demands','I have never felt that work stress affected my performance or relationships',false,true,'{"1":5,"2":5,"3":4,"4":3,"5":1}',0.25),

