(41,'growth_curiosity','Growth Mindset','Which of these two statements is MORE like what you genuinely believe?','attitudinal','choice_best_worst','forced_choice','With enough effort and the right strategies, most skills can be developed significantly','Some people are naturally better suited to certain areas and effort alone has limits',NULL,NULL,NULL,false,false,'{"1":5,"2":2}',0.30),

(42,'growth_curiosity','Intellectual Curiosity','Outside of your direct job requirements, how would you characterise your engagement with learning in the past year?','behavioral_frequency','likert_5','rating_scale','I have done little beyond what my role required','I have done some reading or occasional learning when an interesting topic came up','I have engaged in one or two structured learning activities such as courses or certifications','I have a consistent personal development routine — reading, courses, or communities of practice','I invest significant time and energy in learning beyond my role and can point to specific outcomes',false,false,NULL,0.25),

(43,'growth_curiosity','Feedback Receptivity','You receive detailed critical feedback on a piece of work you are proud of. The feedback is delivered well and seems genuine. Which is most like your reaction?','situational','likert_5','rating_scale','I feel a brief defensive reaction, then genuinely engage with the substance','I appreciate it and immediately ask follow-up questions to understand the specifics','I listen carefully and then take time privately to assess whether it is accurate','I feel motivated by it — this is exactly the kind of input that helps me improve','I am uncomfortable initially but make a point of acting on the specific feedback',false,false,'{"1":4,"2":5,"3":3,"4":5,"5":3}',0.25),

(44,'growth_curiosity','Innovation Tendency','When you have been doing a routine task the same way for several months, what is your most typical pattern?','behavioral_frequency','likert_5','rating_scale','I continue doing it as is — if it works well, there is no reason to change it','I occasionally wonder if there is a better way but rarely pursue it','I periodically review whether it can be improved and sometimes make small changes','I regularly look for improvements and have changed my approach multiple times','I almost always find a way to refine or automate routine tasks',false,false,NULL,0.20),

(45,'growth_curiosity','Growth Mindset','You receive honest feedback that you are weaker than your peers in an area that matters for your career progression. What is your typical thought process over the following week?','situational','likert_5','rating_scale','I feel unsettled initially but develop a specific plan to close the gap','I am motivated to address it and seek out resources or mentors with that skill','I assess whether it is genuinely a priority for my career or if my energy is better elsewhere','I reflect on whether the feedback is accurate before deciding how to respond','I feel energised by it — development gaps are opportunities',false,false,'{"1":4,"2":5,"3":3,"4":2,"5":5}',0.30),

(46,'growth_curiosity','Intellectual Curiosity','Which of these two statements is MORE like how you typically behave?','attitudinal','choice_best_worst','forced_choice','I go deep in my area of expertise and develop genuine mastery','I go broad across multiple areas and connect ideas from different fields',NULL,NULL,NULL,false,false,'{"1":4,"2":5}',0.25),

(47,'growth_curiosity','Feedback Receptivity','How often do you proactively request feedback on your work from colleagues or managers?','behavioral_frequency','likert_5','rating_scale','Rarely — I wait for formal review cycles','Occasionally — when I feel uncertain about something','Regularly — after most significant pieces of work','Frequently — feedback is part of how I calibrate my work','Consistently and systematically — I have a personal practice around seeking feedback',false,false,NULL,0.25),

(48,'growth_curiosity','Innovation Tendency','Which of these two statements is MORE like how you approach your work?','attitudinal','choice_best_worst','forced_choice','I am always looking for what could be done better, even when things are working','I focus on executing the current approach well before exploring changes',NULL,NULL,NULL,false,false,'{"1":5,"2":3}',0.20),

(49,'growth_curiosity','Growth Mindset','You invest significant effort in a project that ultimately fails to achieve its goals despite your best work. Which response most closely reflects your experience?','situational','likert_5','rating_scale','I feel disappointed but find it easier to move on when I can identify what I learned','I am frustrated primarily when the failure was avoidable, but I process it and continue','I treat it as a data point — understanding the failure feels more important than the emotional reaction','I feel resilient about it because I knew outcome uncertainty was part of taking on the work','I am briefly disheartened but recover quickly when I focus on the next challenge',false,false,'{"1":4,"2":3,"3":5,"4":5,"5":4}',0.30),

(50,'growth_curiosity','Intellectual Curiosity','Thinking honestly about your relationship with learning and development, which is most accurate?','attitudinal','likert_5','rating_scale','There are topics or skills I know I should develop but have not prioritised','I have one or two clear development areas I have been slower to address than I should','I am generally proactive about development, though I do not always follow through consistently','I am highly consistent about my own development and rarely delay what I know I should do','I have never knowingly put off a development activity I knew was important for my career',false,true,'{"1":5,"2":5,"3":4,"4":3,"5":1}',0.25);
